Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:49:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Report the idle state of the session with SetIdleHint

logind only knows that a graphical session is idle when the session
says so with SetIdleHint. Nothing in Plasma did, so IdleHint and
IdleSinceHint of a Plasma session stayed false. A program that wants to
know whether the user is idle had to open its own connection to the
display server for KIdleTime.

A new bundled action sets the hint: true after SessionIdleTimeoutSec
without input, false on activity. The setting is in the General group
of powerdevilrc, with no UI. It defaults to 300 seconds, and 0 never
reports the session as idle. It does not depend on the dim and
screen-off settings, because a screen kept on is a display preference
and does not mean that the user is present.

The hint goes to the session that the policy agent already holds, so it
reaches ConsoleKit as well as logind. A ConsoleKit session has the same
SetIdleHint method. With logind, that session is the one that
GetSession("auto") gives the policy agent: its own session, or the
graphical session of the user when PowerDevil runs outside one.

The action only reports the idle state. The inhibitions keep acting on
PowerDevil's own actions.

Ultramarine: the MR's other commit, 7831b2f7 "policyagent: also inhibit
the logind idle action", is deliberately left out. It adds idle to
PowerDevil's own logind block inhibitor, which it holds for the whole
session. checkLogindInhibitions() mirrors every other block inhibitor
in ListInhibitors, skipping only its own PID, and maps idle to
ChangeScreenSettings. With two Plasma sessions (fast user switching),
each PowerDevil would then pick up the other one's lock, and not dim
or turn off the screen while its session is unlocked. Without it, a
logind IdleAction= other than the default ignore can act on the hint.

BUG: 448942

Backported from https://invent.kde.org/plasma/powerdevil/-/merge_requests/699
(commit bc11bfa0 only, onto v6.8.2).
